{
  "title": "Check residual symbol-gap dependence after preserving local text rates",
  "statement": "The 615 matched certain paragraph lines on 31 public pages give average pooled Pearson gap autocorrelations of 0.04458 in ZL and 0.04485 in Takahashi over lags 11–40. Global word shuffling brings the means to about zero (one-sided p=0.005 in both). Shuffling intact lines within each page gives means of 0.04755 and 0.04780, with one-sided p=0.975 and 0.985. Shuffling words within paragraphs gives means of 0.04934 and 0.04944, both p=1. The pinned page-local self-citation medians exceed the manuscript values. The stationary whole-line copy medians are around 0.003. After centering gap lengths within pages, the observed aggregate is about −0.014 and the paragraph-word shuffle p-values are 0.710 and 0.565. In gap-only controls, alternating page rates alone yield 24 of 24 global rejections and 1 of 24 page-centered rejections. Rank-imposed AR dependence gets 0 of 24 page-centered rejections at either rate setting. A separate exact lag-20 recurrence gets 24 of 24 page-centered rejections with equal rates and 22 of 24 with alternating rates. These results distinguish a pooled long-lag effect from residual long-lag dependence relative to the tested local controls, with demonstrated sensitivity to the specific recurrence used in the positive control.",
  "program": "L2",
  "check": "Freeze separate estimands for short-lag and long-lag correlations. Build public text controls with the manuscript's page and paragraph layout and introduce controlled shifts in glyph frequency, explicit lagged recurrence, and a range of weaker burst processes at constant mean rates. Compare within-page and within-paragraph conditioned baselines without changing the order of paragraphs. Report the power of each conditional test for the specified alternatives and its false-positive rate under known rate shifts.",
  "on_path": false,
  "hard": true,
  "source": {
    "url": "https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0260948",
    "where": "Periodicity of symbols and Tables 3–4"
  },
  "practice": {
    "selection": "Use the intersection of eligible P lines by ID from public practice ZL and Takahashi. Require each line to be nonempty with certain words made of acdefghiklmnopqrsty. Retain selected lines in original order and join words with single spaces within and between lines and pages for pooled estimates. Use ASCII EVA characters and fixed assay symbols acdehiklnoqrsty plus space, with at least 101 gaps in every evaluated case.",
    "measurement": "For each symbol compute differences of adjacent occurrence indices and Pearson correlations between gap vectors shifted by lags 1 through 40. Pooling uses a concatenation of pages. The page-centered version uses only gaps wholly within a page, subtracts each page's mean for that symbol, and pools within-page cross products and sum of squares at each lag. Use pages with more than lag plus one gaps and at least 25 aggregated pairs. Average coefficients equally across lags and across symbols.",
    "text_nulls": "Use 199 Python Random(71430) permutations for each text null, with global reassignment of words to fixed slots, intact line shuffling within pages, and word reassignment inside paragraph blocks in each page using the IVTFF opening/closing markers. Report one-sided larger-or-equal Monte Carlo p-values with plus-one correction. The fixed paragraph blocks preserve word counts and the inventories of each paragraph. Recombining words changes local character neighborhoods.",
    "copy_controls": "Use seeds 81–86 for both pinned G-self-citation, with exact certain-token line counts, and the reconstructed P-R-009 single-table whole-copy generator, with its two line streams and synthetic line lengths. Both fit public practice-training pages only and use the selected practice line IDs for evaluation.",
    "simulation": "Each run has 31 blocks of 120 gaps. Simulate independent geometric gaps with p=0.135 or alternating p=0.07 and p=0.24 by block. A correlated version rank-reorders the same gaps within each block by a standard Gaussian AR(1) with rho 0.92. Independently, the lag-20 check repeats the first 20 gaps of every 40-gap block. Use 24 NumPy default_rng seeds beginning at 61500 for the factorial and 47700 for the lag-20 check. Compare pooled means with 99 global gap shuffles and page-centered means with 99 within-block shuffles. These calibration cases use simulated gap vectors.",
    "coefficient_order_in_copy_seed_results": [
      "pooled lags 1–40",
      "pooled lags 11–40",
      "page-centered lags 1–40",
      "page-centered lags 11–40"
    ],
